Subject: [PATCH] loot: a key or a quest item is not left for a nearly full bag

WHY THIS PATCH EXISTS

mod-overseer#1424. StoreLootAction::Execute skips every item that does not
stack (max stack 1) once the bot's "bag space" reads over 80 percent, for a
bot whose master is not a real player. Every family member is such a bot:
its master carries a PlayerbotAI too, so IsRealPlayer() is false.

Two kinds of item it skips that way should never be:

  * A KEY. It goes to the keyring (bag family mask 0x100), which BagSpaceValue
    (src/Ai/Base/Value/StatsValues.cpp:203) does not count at all, so a bag
    80 percent full says nothing about whether it fits. Blackrock Depths'
    Prison Cell Key (11140, High Interrogator Gerstahn, 100 percent) opens
    the eight Detention Block cell doors (lock 699) on the route to
    Houndmaster Grebmar for a party with no lockpicker.
  * A QUEST ITEM. Ironfel (10999, Fineous Darkvire) is the one item between
    a family and the Shadowforge Key (quest 3802). IsLootAllowed already
    says yes to it for the quest in the log; the bag shortcut then drops it.

Measured on the dev realm, 2026-11-08, "bag space" as BagSpaceValue computes
it for the family with no rogue: 86, 81, 82, 67 and 94 percent. Four of five
would leave both items on the corpse.

WHAT IT CHANGES

The 80 percent shortcut does not apply to an item that goes to the keyring
or is a quest item (class 12 or bonding BIND_QUEST_ITEM). Everything else is
as before. Nothing is forced: CMSG_AUTOSTORE_LOOT_ITEM still goes through the
core's own store check, which refuses an item there is no room for.

WHAT WOULD LET THIS PATCH BE DELETED

Upstream exempting keyring and quest items from the bag-space shortcut, or
the shortcut asking the core (CanStoreNewItem) instead of a percentage.

APPLIES TO

    mod-playerbots @ 40884e9c135c1daf27ffd894a6047502a5701130
    src/Ai/Base/Actions/LootAction.cpp, StoreLootAction::Execute
    Replayed by tests/replay_loot_key_bag_space.py against the pinned file
    (tests/fixtures/loot_key/LootAction.cpp).

diff --git a/src/Ai/Base/Actions/LootAction.cpp b/src/Ai/Base/Actions/LootAction.cpp
index d8a50e4..e56f3c9 100644
--- a/src/Ai/Base/Actions/LootAction.cpp
+++ b/src/Ai/Base/Actions/LootAction.cpp
@@ -430,7 +430,14 @@ bool StoreLootAction::Execute(Event event)
         if (!proto)
             continue;
 
-        if (!IsRealPlayer(botAI->GetMaster()) && AI_VALUE(uint8, "bag space") > 80)
+        // A key goes to the keyring, which "bag space" does not count, and a
+        // quest item is the reason the corpse was opened at all (mod-overseer
+        // #1424): neither is left behind for a nearly full bag. The core
+        // still refuses one there is no room for.
+        bool const takenAnyway = (proto->BagFamily & BAG_FAMILY_MASK_KEYS) != 0 ||
+                                 proto->Class == ITEM_CLASS_QUEST ||
+                                 proto->Bonding == BIND_QUEST_ITEM;
+        if (!takenAnyway && !IsRealPlayer(botAI->GetMaster()) && AI_VALUE(uint8, "bag space") > 80)
         {
             uint32 maxStack = proto->GetMaxStackSize();
             if (maxStack == 1)
